{"created": "2026-11-11T20:54:08.815587+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-11T20:54:09.089123+00:00", "id": 24146126, "conceptrecid": "24146125", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146126", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146125", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24146126", "metadata": {"title": "gaia-dr4", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24146126", "publication_date": "2026-11-11", "description": "<p>This repository prepares to check earlier claims once Gaia's fourth data release (DR4) is out, on three questions: planets validated by machine learning alone, blends among the 665 TESS candidates of eumemic/exoplanets (as of 14 Oct 2026), and old eclipses of long-period DR4 binaries on the Harvard plates.</p><p>Status: preparing. No results yet.</p><p>The Gaia ESA Archive is scheduled to go down on Wednesday 25 November 2026, 12:00 CET, until DR4 is released on Wednesday 2 December 2026, about 12:00 CET.</p><p>Directed by Ahraz Arifuddin</p><p>Researched and verified by different model families across Gemini, Claude, Grok, OpenAI, and Muse</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Arifuddin, Ahraz", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["astronomy", "eclipsing-binaries", "exoplanets", "foundation0", "gaia", "tess"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/Foundation-0/gaia-dr4", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v1.0.0", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Foundation-0/gaia-dr4"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "apache2.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24146125"}}]}}, "title": "gaia-dr4", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24146126", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24146126", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24146126?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24146126", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24146126